{"_id":"6a2fef432204ffbc59e5a320","roadmapSlug":"python-data-analysis","nodeId":"7ukR74cN6lHbvhs4mFn6R","description":"# args & kwargs\n\n`*args` allows a function to accept any number of positional arguments as a tuple. `**kwargs` allows any number of keyword arguments as a dictionary. They make functions flexible when the number or names of arguments are not known in advance, and are widely used in Python libraries for passing options through layers of function calls.","resources":[{"type":"article","title":"Args and Kwargs in Python ΓÇô Function Calling Made Easy","url":"https://towardsdatascience.com/args-and-kwargs-in-python-function-calling-made-easy-acfe736f988a/","_id":"6a75d326b0650226a50aebec"},{"type":"article","title":"Python args & kwargs","url":"https://www.w3schools.com/python/python_args_kwargs.asp","_id":"6a75d326b0650226a50aebed"},{"type":"video","title":"Python *ARGS & **KWARGS are awesome!","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Vh__2V2tXUM","_id":"6a75d326b0650226a50aebee"}],"createdAt":"2026-06-15T12:25:39.099Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-07T12:44:22.099Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[{"_id":"6a5e3360acf8c05faf5e1c2a","title":"DataCamp - Data Analyst with Python","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/QY0dY9"},{"_id":"6a5e3365acf8c05faf5e1ded","title":"DataCamp - Python Data Fundamentals","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/k4V24x"}],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/python-data-analysis/content/7ukR74cN6lHbvhs4mFn6R.md"}